

-> What is Spring MVC & why it is used?
    Spring MVC (Model–View–Controller) is a web framework used to build web applications and REST APIs.
    In Spring Boot, we mainly use Spring MVC to:
    Handle HTTP requests (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
    Map URLs to controller methods
    Convert JSON ↔ Java objects
    Send structured HTTP responses
    📌 Why used in Spring Boot?
    Clean separation of layers
    Annotation-based (less boilerplate)
    Perfect for REST APIs (microservices)

-> Role of DispatcherServlet
    DispatcherServlet is the front controller of Spring MVC.
    👉 Every request goes through it first
    Responsibilities:
    Receives HTTP request
    Finds correct controller method
    Handles data binding
    Returns response
    📌 Think of it as Traffic Police 🚦 for requests.

-> Complete Request–Response Lifecycle
    Client sends HTTP request
    Request hits DispatcherServlet
    Dispatcher finds controller method
    Controller executes business logic
    Response object created
    Response converted to JSON
    HTTP response sent to client

-> How Spring Boot auto-configures Spring MVC
    Spring Boot:
    Detects spring-boot-starter-web
    Auto-registers DispatcherServlet
    Configures Jackson, validation, converters
    Sets default error handling
    📌 No XML, no manual config needed ✅
